      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 114,
      "outputTokens": 862,
      "costUsd": 0.007815,
      "pronunciationText": "The mode is the value where the density is highest. Here's why X is most likely to be found near there. Slide a narrow window, two tenths wide, along the hump. It catches the most area, and so the most probability, near the top of this symmetric hump. Near one, it catches about zero point one five, and near zero point two, about zero point zero five. So the mode is at the peak of f, not of F. F only builds up probability, so its top doesn't tell you where f peaks."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-03",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-s06/scene-03.wav",
      "durationInFrames": 1043,
      "worstWordGap": {
