      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 117,
      "outputTokens": 869,
      "costUsd": 0.0078795,
      "pronunciationText": "Finding the peak is a maximum problem, like the ones you've solved before. Write f as six x minus three x squared, over four. Its derivative is six minus six x, over four, which is zero at x equals one. The second derivative is minus three halves, which is negative, so that's a maximum. The mode is one, where the density is three quarters. And because this hump is symmetric about one, half the area lies on each side, so the median is one as well. F of one is a half, which checks it."
    },
