      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 95,
      "outputTokens": 699,
      "costUsd": 0.0063384999999999995,
      "pronunciationText": "But a density doesn't always have a stationary point. For the cookie, x over eight, from zero to four, the derivative is one eighth, and it's never zero. The density keeps climbing, so its greatest value is at the right-hand end, the edge of the cookie. The mode is four. So, just like any global maximum, check the endpoints as well. And if a density is completely flat, it has no single mode."
    },
