      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 140,
      "outputTokens": 998,
      "costUsd": 0.009052000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the middle. The median, m, is the value with half the probability below it. That's an area on f, but F already holds the areas. So we solve F of m equals one half. For the cookie, F of x is the fraction of the cookie within x of the centre, pi x squared over pi times sixteen, which is x squared over sixteen. Integrating x over eight from zero gives the same. So m squared over sixteen is a half, m squared is eight, and m is two root two, about two point eight three. The negative root, minus two root two, is outside zero to four, so we reject it, and say so."
    },
