      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 126,
      "outputTokens": 1024,
      "costUsd": 0.009279,
      "pronunciationText": "The quartiles split the probability into quarters. The lower quartile solves F equals one quarter, and the upper quartile solves F equals three quarters. Here, the lower quartile is two, and the upper quartile is two root three, about three point four six. Now look at the cookie. Circles at two, two point eight three and three point four six cut it into four pieces of equal area. In this sample cookie, each holds fifteen of its sixty chips. A real cookie would only come close. The pieces get narrower towards the edge, because the density is higher there. A quarter of the probability fits into less width."
    },
