      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 900,
      "costUsd": 0.008164,
      "pronunciationText": "Try one more. A density is three x squared over eight, from zero to two, and its F is x cubed over eight. The density keeps increasing, so the mode is at the end, at two. For the median, x cubed over eight equals a half, so x cubed is four, and m is the cube root of four, about one point five nine. In the same way, the lower quartile is the cube root of two, about one point two six. The median is well left of the mode. The density is low near zero, so it takes a lot of width there to collect half the probability."
    },
