      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 143,
      "outputTokens": 1231,
      "costUsd": 0.0111505,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's why the difference matters in a real problem. A component's lifetime, L hours, has density three times four minus l, all squared, over sixty four, for l from zero to four. That density is highest at zero and falls the whole way, so the mode is zero. Its F is one minus four minus l, cubed, over sixty four. Setting F equal to a half gives four minus m, cubed, equals thirty two. So m is four minus the cube root of thirty two, about zero point eight three hours. Half of these components fail in under fifty minutes, even though some last up to four hours. The most likely lifetime and the median answer different questions."
    },
