      "costUsd": 0.0062715,
      "pronunciationText": "Solve F of x equals one quarter. So x squared plus two x equals two. Complete the square: x plus one, all squared, is three, so x is minus one, plus or minus root three. Minus one minus root three is outside zero to two, so reject it. The lower quartile is root three minus one, about zero point seven three. Keeping both roots is wrong. Only one is in the domain."
